Represents each individual transaction line inside a bank statement, used as the source of truth for bank reconciliation against accounting entries.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Store imported or manual bank transactions (debits, credits, fees, interest)
Bank reconciliation (match with payments, invoices, or manual journal items)
Handle multi-currency transactions and currency differences
Support auto-matching rules and reconciliation widgets
Generate bank transaction reports and cash flow analysis

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
statement_id → account.bank.statement (required)
date (date, required), amount (monetary, can be positive/negative)
payment_ref / ref (char), narration (text)
partner_id → res.partner
account_id → account.account (when not reconciled)
journal_id (related from statement)
foreign_currency_id, amount_currency
Many2many: move_line_ids → account.move.line (reconciled lines)
Computed: is_reconciled, running_balance

Critical Hooks: action_reconcile, _compute_amount, button_undo_reconciliation, reconcile_bank_lines
Security: Inherited from parent statement + account manager rights

RAG Routing Keywords:
bank statement line, statement transaction, reconcile line, unreconciled bank line, bank feed line, imported transaction, bank statement detail, matching bank line, statement line amount, payment reference, bank recon line
Related Models (most joined):

account.bank.statement (parent)
account.move.line (via reconciliation)
account.payment
res.partner
account.journal
account.account

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.bank.statement.line is the transactional child model of account.bank.statement that stores every bank movement with date, amount, payment_ref, partner_id, and currency details. It serves as the main source for bank reconciliation, linking to account.move.line through move_line_ids, enabling automatic and manual matching of bank transactions with accounting entries, payments, and invoices in Odoo’s accounting and cash management flows.